--- 4. macOS ships no font named Roboto (this host) ---
$ ls /System/Library/Fonts | grep -i roboto
(no output)
exit: 1

$ ls /System/Library/Fonts/Supplemental | grep -i roboto
(no output)
exit: 1

$ ls ~/Library/Fonts /Library/Fonts 2>/dev/null | grep -i roboto
(no output)
exit: 1

Empty output above (grep exit 1 = no match): an unbundled
fontFamily: 'Roboto' had nothing to resolve to on macOS, and the engine
fell back silently while the ThemeData still reported the name.

--- Not established here ---
Android and iOS device rendering. No device or emulator is attached to
this environment, so the Android claim rests on the framework itself
naming Roboto, unbundled, for android/fuchsia - i.e. Flutter relies on
the platform providing it - and the iOS claim rests on iOS shipping the
San Francisco system faces, not Roboto. Neither claim is load-bearing
for this fix: the fix is that the design system no longer overrides
whatever the framework chose.
